Third-party work
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The Hunter SmartPort (REM line) driver in firmware/lib/hunter/ and
firmware/src/hunter_bus.cpp is adapted from the HunterRoam library as used in
isprinklr_esp (v1). The frame layout, bitfield packing and pulse timings come
from that code. Its lineage:

  HunterRoam (Hunter Roam - WiFi)
    Copyright (C) 2020-2022 Eloi Codina Torras
    https://github.com/ecodina/hunter-wifi
    License: GPL-3.0-or-later

  which is adapted from:

  OpenSprinkler-Firmware-Hunter (hunter.cpp)
    Sebastien, https://github.com/seb821/OpenSprinkler-Firmware-Hunter
    A fork of OpenSprinkler firmware, Copyright (C) 2015 Ray Wang,
    License: GPL-3.0-or-later (LICENSE.txt is GPLv3; source headers grant
    "version 3 of the License, or (at your option) any later version")

  and the original SmartPort reverse-engineering by Dave Fleck and
  Scott Shumate:
    https://www.hackster.io/sshumate/hunter-sprinkler-wifi-remote-control-4ea918

The v2 code is a rewrite (pure frame builder and pulse encoder, FreeRTOS bus
task) rather than a copy, but it reproduces the upstream encoding byte for byte
and is distributed under the same license.

